      "revision": 1373460516,
      "text": "Ficus palmata, commonly known as Punjab fig or \"Bedu\", is a species of flowering plant in the family Moraceae. It is a shrub or tree native to southern Egypt to north-eastern tropical Africa and the Arabian Peninsula, and southeastern Iran to Afghanistan, Pakistan, northern India, and Nepal. It has edible fruit."
